 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 238597,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/e48869432d20f231.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Kerstin Uvnäs-Moberg, et al./BMC Pregnancy and Childbirth, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows oxytocin levels during labor. Oxytocyin is a hormone that causes contraction of the muscles around the uterus.</p>\n<p>Make a claim based on this graph.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 744125,
     "content_html": "The muscles contract at the start of the labor and never relax. The single contraction gets gradually stronger."
    },
    {
     "id": 744124,
     "content_html": "The muscles contract at the start of the labor and never relax. The single contraction gets gradually weaker."
    },
    {
     "id": 744123,
     "content_html": "Contractions happen at intervals. Muscles contract for a few minutes and then relax. Each contraction is stronger than the previous one."
    },
    {
     "id": 744126,
     "content_html": "Contractions happen at intervals. Muscles contract for a few minutes and then relax. Contractions change in magnitude."
    }
   ],
